{
  "name": "Unified Invoice Archiving — v3 (safe multi-PDF)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# Unified Invoice Archiving v3\n### Gmail → PDF → Validation → SFTP + Google Sheets\n\n**Purpose**  Automatically archive invoice PDFs and register invoice metadata without relying on an LLM.\n\n**Supported providers**  Octopus Energy (electricity/gas), Dimensione, Google Cloud, Hetzner.\n\n**Flow**\n1. Start manually or on the schedule.\n2. Retrieve matching Gmail messages and split PDF attachments into individual items.\n3. Extract PDF text, identify provider and validate invoice fields.\n4. Route to the provider's SFTP folder and Google Sheets worksheet.\n5. Keep the source email; successful paths end at the Completed nodes.\n\n**First-time setup**\n- Connect **Gmail OAuth2**, **SFTP**, and **Google Sheets service account** credentials.\n- Set the Gmail sender query and `newer_than:450d` lookback window.\n- Configure each provider's SFTP target directory in **Parse invoice and canonical name**.\n- Verify Google Sheets document IDs, tabs and matching columns in all four upsert nodes.\n- Run the **Manual Trigger** with representative invoices for every provider before activating the schedule.\n\n**Operational notes**\n- Only text-based PDFs are supported; scanned PDFs need OCR.\n- Emails are **not deleted**.\n- SFTP uploads and Sheets writes are not atomic. Reprocessing can rewrite a file at the same path.\n- There is no durable exactly-once registry or centralized error alerting. Configure an n8n Error Workflow and monitor executions.\n- This export has not been validated against live accounts. Keep the workflow inactive until testing is complete.",
        "height": 1000,
        "width": 636,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "46e1ffc5-aea7-4e34-9c5d-ef228a214990",
      "name": "00 — WORKFLOW OVERVIEW",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        880,
        -512
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 01 · Start\n**Manual Trigger** — run a controlled test.\n\n**Schedule Trigger** — periodic mailbox polling. Verify the interval before activation; keep the workflow inactive while testing.\n\n**Tip:** avoid simultaneous manual and scheduled runs when processing the same backlog.",
        "height": 578,
        "width": 362,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "50e5294b-75cd-42df-b1d9-68c27dd3aefb",
      "name": "01 — TRIGGERS",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1552,
        -128
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 02 · Gmail intake\n**Gmail - Get invoice messages** filters the four sender addresses and retrieves attachments.\n\n**Setup:** connect Gmail OAuth2; review sender addresses, `filename:pdf` and the 450-day backfill window.\n\n**Keep messages with attachments** excludes messages without binary attachments.\n\n**Normalize PDF binary** splits eligible PDFs into separate items. Non-PDF attachments are ignored.\n\n**Security:** Gmail sender filters alone do not establish invoice authenticity; verify unexpected senders and attachments.",
        "height": 578,
        "width": 904,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "a926d6ba-2026-4d58-ac75-89687686cebb",
      "name": "02 — GMAIL INTAKE",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1936,
        -128
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 03 · PDF extraction and validation\n**Extract PDF text** reads text-based PDFs (no OCR).\n\n**Parse invoice and canonical name** identifies the provider, extracts invoice number, date and amount, and produces a canonical filename and SFTP path.\n\n**Hetzner:** validates net + VAT against gross total.\n\n**Failure:** missing or ambiguous required fields stop execution. Inspect n8n Executions and adjust the provider parser; do not silently archive invalid records.",
        "height": 578,
        "width": 638,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "fc954940-c150-411d-b3db-0366be3f6305",
      "name": "03 — EXTRACT & VALIDATE",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2864,
        -128
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 04 — STORAGE & COMPLETION\n\nAll four provider branches share the same processing pattern:\n\n1. **Filter** — route the parsed invoice to its provider branch.\n2. **SFTP upload** — save the PDF to its configured destination.\n3. **Restore parsed item** — preserve the invoice metadata and binary data after upload.\n4. **Google Sheets upsert** — create or update the invoice record.\n5. **Completed** — finish without deleting the source Gmail message.\n\n**Providers:** Octopus Energy, Dimensione, Google Cloud, Hetzner.\n\n**Setup:** verify each SFTP destination, Google Sheets document/tab, service-account permissions, and provider filters before enabling the schedule.\n\n**Important:** a Sheets upsert is not a preventive SFTP duplicate check. Test repeated runs and verify uploads and sheet rows. Emails remain in Gmail.",
        "height": 1088,
        "width": 1266,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "524d0142-afdd-468f-8894-926c781d7d7d",
      "name": "04 — STORAGE & COMPLETION",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        3520,
        -336
      ]
    },
